    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/program-manager-employer-relations-experiential-learning-houston-texas-united-states-121ee067-3020-4b34-a1f4-8be67a2d6bd1": {
      "title": "Recommended postings",
      "description": "Program Manager, Employer Relations/Experiential Learning - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Program Manager, Employer Relations/Experiential Learning 496836 Full-Time Center for Career Development Add to favorites View favorites Department : Center for Career Development Salary : Commensurate with education and experience. Description : The Program Manager of Employer Relations and Experiential Learning develops and maintains relationships with potential employers of UHCL students. This position is responsible for devising strategies and plans to support the recruitment of employer partners, identifying and supporting placements for student internships, industry projects, and other experiential learning opportunities. The Program Manager oversees the planning, coordination, and execution of all on-campus recruiting events, including job fairs, career weeks, networking events, and workshops to support students in their job search efforts. Duties: Develops relationships with employers to increase experiential learning opportunities for UHCL students. Oversees internships, Hawk Job Shadow Program, and Corporate Partners Program in collaboration with the Director. Maintains relationships with existing corporate recruiters through employer visits, telephone calls, email, and face-to-face communication. Oversees strategic planning and assessment for employer outreach and development. Responsible for the supervision, training, and professional development of assigned student employee(s). Oversees social media and events student support staff ensuring events are posted in a timely manner while adhering to the established social media marketing strategy. In collaboration with the Director, leads campus marketing activities for employer-related events and activities to ensure marketing materials are available through various communication channels. Develops and manages systems for collecting information and reporting experiential learning outcomes and measurements to stakeholders. Contributes to identifying new opportunities for students in disciplines that do not currently include work-integrated learning. Oversees the planning, coordination, and execution of all departmental events, including major career fairs, career weeks, networking events, and similar events and programs. In collaboration with the Associate Director, manages the departmental events calendar. In collaboration with career coaches, develops employer led workshops on career readiness topics and delivers programming designed to inform and educate students on a broad range of career pathways. Oversees Jobs4Hawks student registration and initiates marketing campaigns for activation and profile completion. Leads training on Jobs4Hawks database while monitoring access for faculty and staff. Oversees all incoming employer communications. Attends staff and University meetings and professional conferences/meetings. Covers required evening and weekend hours and performs other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in education, business, social sciences, communication, public administration, or a related field. Minimum three years of experience working, developing, and maintaining relationships with employers and other community organizations. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in higher education administration, student affairs, educational leadership, business administration, public administration, or a related field. Previous experience supporting career services, career programs, and or job placement for students at a college or university career center. Previous supervisory experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of job search strategies, labor market supply/demand, and employer's recruitment and interviewing methodologies. Ability to understand the employer engagement process, including the importance of the initial conversation and active listening. Knowledge of student engagement and career services products and platforms. Skills in utilizing student engagement platforms, or client-based CRMs to run reports and analyze data. Ability to assess and problem solve effectively to address employer needs and formulate solutions. Skills in Microsoft Office, specifically Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Ability to effectively express thoughts and ideas verbally and through written communication. Knowledge of supervisory best practices and staff development. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Associate Dean, College of Education 496874 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Program Manager, Employer Relations/Experiential Learning 496836 Student Affairs-Student Engagement Full-Time Division of Student Affairs Office Supervisor 496855 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Visiting Assistant Professor, Healthcare Administration 496842 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Business Full-Time College of Business College Business Administrator 496835 VP, Admin & Finance-Business Operations Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities Director, Grants and Services 496814 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of HSH Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities 281–283–7600 2700 Bay Area Boulevard, Houston, TX 77058 © 2026 University of Houston–Clear Lake Maps and Directions Emergency Information University of Houston System University Police Fraud & Non-Compliance Hotline Campus Safety Directory Human Resources TRAIL (Statewide Search) State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Public Information Act Fraud Reporting Compact with Texans Linking Notice Privacy Notice University Policies Report It Faculty and Course Profiles Emergency Resource Card Texas 