      "title": "Recommended postings",
      "description": "Office Supervisor - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Office Supervisor 496855 Full-Time Dean of Education Add to favorites View favorites Department : Dean of Education Salary : Commensurate with Experience and Education Description : The Office Supervisor is responsible for providing high-level office support and supervision of other support staff in an area or office. Work may include compiling information, data entry, coordinating activities, checking documents for accuracy, and overseeing financial matters. Also responsible for being familiar with the functions, practices, and policies of the organizational unit to which assigned. Works under limited supervision, with considerable latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. Duties: Coordinates supply orders, vendor payments, and PCard. Produces accurate financial records and ensures adherence to University purchasing guidelines. Processes POIs, ePARs, payroll changes, and reconciles PCard transactions for CEP programs. Ensures accuracy and compliance, resulting in timely financial processing that supports program operations and audit readiness. Resolves issues and answers inquiries regarding policies and procedures. Provides supervision of staff, including defining job duties, overseeing employee performance, providing guidance and support, and communicating organizational needs in accordance with the University's objectives, policies, and applicable laws. Trains office support staff, temporary employees, and student workers. Tracks expenditures, monitors accounts, and prepares budget reports for CEP leadership. Provides reliable data to guide decision-making, resource allocation, and grant management, and performs other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED Minimum of five years of office support experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of accounting and financial management processes preferably in an education setting (e.g., payroll, purchasing, reconciliations). Knowledge of Human Resources processes including POIs, ePARs, and onboarding procedures. Knowledge of university policies and compliance standards related to fiscal accountability and audit readiness. Skilled in Microsoft Office/365, particularly Excel and Outlook, for managing budgets, reports, and communications. Skilled in maintaining accurate records, preparing financial reports, and processing transactions. Supervisory skills to manage and lead staff. Ability to manage multiple deadlines, tasks, and program needs simultaneously with accuracy. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing, with staff, faculty, students, and external partners. Ability to handle sensitive financial and personnel information with confidentiality and integrity. Possess an understanding of workflow optimization and efficiency in financial and administrative systems. All positions at the University of Houston System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Associate Dean, College of Education 496874 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Program Manager, Employer Relations/Experiential Learning 496836 Student Affairs-Student Engagement Full-Time Division of Student Affairs Office Supervisor 496855 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Visiting Assistant Professor, Healthcare Administration 496842 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of Business Full-Time College of Business College Business Administrator 496835 VP, Admin & Finance-Business Operations Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities Director, Grants and Services 496814 Sr Vice Pres & Provost-College of HSH Full-Time College of Human Sciences and Humanities 281–283–7600 2700 Bay Area Boulevard, Houston, 