      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Executive Assistant 496538 Full-Time Office of the Provost Add to favorites View favorites Department : Office of the Provost Salary : Commensurate with experience and education Description: The Executive Assistant to the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost is responsible for providing complex professional and administrative support to the executive by managing office staff and acting as a liaison with reporting departments, institutions, or other contacts. Work includes coordinating communications, activities, and high-level operations. Participates in the planning and implementation of initiatives for a large division. Duties: Serves as the primary administrative liaison for the Vice President or Sr. Vice President, coordinating communications and collaborating with internal and external stakeholders. May prepare notices or agendas for meetings and hearings for the Senior Vice President. Coordinates calendars, meetings, and other activities with internal and external professionals and community relationships on behalf of the Vice President or Sr. Vice President. Performs data analysis, prepares spreadsheets, runs PeopleSoft financial reports, and reviews management methods in order to improve workflow, simplify procedures, and implement cost reduction. Secures the orderly processing of documents, orders, and other forms according to standard approved procedures while maintaining confidential records and executive files. Oversees administrative office staff, delegates assignments, and supervises all work, assuring the highest quality standards. Participates in the coordination of a wide variety of special projects and/or assignments and performs other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Associate's degree Minimum seven years of executive-level administrative support experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of office-related business practices and procedures, university policies, and organizational structure. Ability to exercise discretion, confidentiality, and judgment when dealing with sensitive issues. Knowledge of Microsoft Suite (Word, Excel, etc.) as well as virtual platforms such as Teams. Ability to handle high-level administrative issues. Proficient interpersonal and communication skills in interacting with a broad range of internal and external constituents. Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgment and act upon decisions within the scope of delegated authority. Ability to build collaborative relationships and provide exceptional customer service. Analytical skills to ascertain problems, identify solutions, and handle interruptions. All positions at the University of Houston System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Pr