    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/senior-client-server-database-analyst-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Client Server Database Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Client Server Database Analyst - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Senior Client Server Database Analyst 496900 Full-Time Information Technology Add to favorites View favorites Department : Information Technology Salary : Commensurate with Experience and Education Description : The Senior Client Server Database Analyst works as part of the Business Application team to lead, design, and develop web-enabled client-server applications and application infrastructure software using a variety of software development tools and database technologies. Is an application lead with the user community to develop application specifications and design web-enabled consumer applications to support university business practices. Pursuant to the State of Texas Executive Order No. GA-48, this position researches, works on, or has access to critical infrastructure and requires the ability to maintain the security or integrity of the University infrastructure. This position requires personnel to be routinely reviewed to determine whether or not criminal history or continuous connections for the government or political apparatus of a foreign adversary might prevent the employee from being able to maintain the security or integrity of the infrastructure. Duties: Leads, designs, and develops client-server applications. Analyzes data and comes up with analytics to support student success. Develops and maintains applications as well as dashboards. Prepares program documentation, user documentation, and project plans and provides user training, including one-on-one and organized group classes. Attends professional training, including attendance at seminars, organized classes, and one-on-one training with other team members. Prepares reports and updates status as requested and performs related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer science, mathematics, or related field. Three years of technical and analytical experience developing data models, data mining, and segmentation techniques. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in computer science. Progressive experience in general technology skills in areas such as IT infrastructure, data preparation, data engineering, ML operationalization, and data and analytics governance. Experience in dashboarding, data modeling, and data analytics. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Working knowledge of data analysis. Ability to derive meaningful data analytics using multiple data sources. Ability to research technical problems to the lowest level and come up with a solution. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to analyze software requests to determine the requirements of the requests. All positions at the University of Houston System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 2:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 2:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Pr