      "title": "Manager, IT Project",
      "description": "Manager, IT Project - Houston, Texas, United States UHS Home Job Search My Profile Kiosk mode Manager, IT Project 496877 Full-Time Information Technology Add to favorites View favorites Department : Information Technology Salary : Commensurate with education and experience. Description : Under general supervision, provides project leadership and support for information technology project teams - from project initiation through completion. Assignments are typically small projects or components of mid- to large scale projects related to implementation of new or revised information management systems. Project teams are comprised of technical experts, functional area subject matter experts and project managers. Duties: Leads or participates, depending on project size, in defining project goals, objectives, scope and estimates for schedules, resources and costs. Supports project execution through ongoing coordination of planning, task assignments, performance reporting, change management, risk management and issue resolution. Coordinates communications among project teams, customers and appropriate levels of management. Prepares project schedules, timelines; monitor project and technical team's progress to ensure stakeholders remain engaged where appropriate. Works in conjunction with functional sponsors, technical subject matter experts, and/or business analysts to gather project requirements. Prepares and deliver project status reports and presentations using approved enterprise reporting tools. May provide input to the formulating and managing project budgets. Participates in the acquisition process for project-related goods and contracted services and perform additional duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business administration or related discipline. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in managing multiple simple to complex IT projects. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of project management lifecycle. Ability to communicate fluently and professionally, both verbally and in writing. Knowledge of various methods for eliciting and documenting requirements. Ability to manage differing perspectives among use groups, negotiate resolutions, and prioritize completing needs. Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects at once. Ability to identify issues and problems, and communicate complex information clearly, concisely, manage complex issues and facilitate resolution. Ability to address faculty, staff, and student concerns with a service-oriented approach. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and data visualization tools, including Microsoft Power BI, MS Project and MS Visio. Ability to influence, develop and lead multidisciplinary teams to achieve established objectives. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospac